@{
}

<div class="columns">
    <div class="column is-8">
        <div class="content">
            <h2 class="is-size-6">Advanced settings</h2>
            <p>These settings are typically administred by the RP but for demo purposes we expose them to you for testing behaviours and browser support</p>
            <form id="options">
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Attestation type</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-attestation">
                                <option selected value="none">None</option>
                                <option value="indirect">Indirect</option>
                                <option value="direct">Direct</option>
                                <option value="enterprise">Enterprise</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Authenticator</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-authenticator">
                                <option selected value="">Not specified</option>
                                <option value="cross-platform">Cross Platform (Token)</option>
                                <option value="platform">Platform (TPM)</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">User verification</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-userverification">
                                <option value="required">Required</option>
                                <option selected value="preferred">Preferred</option>
                                <option value="discouraged">Discouraged</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">UserVerification can be changed for both register & login</p>

                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Resident Key</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-residentkey">
                                <option value="required">Required</option>
                                <option selected value="preferred">Preferred</option>
                                <option value="discouraged">Discouraged</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">For register the client will guide the user through setting up user verification if needed to create a discoverable credential. This takes precedence over the setting of userVerification.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Algorithms</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-7" checked /> ES256 <span class="has-text-grey">(-7)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-257" checked /> RS256 <span class="has-text-grey">(-257)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-8" checked /> EdDSA <span class="has-text-grey">(-8)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-35" /> ES384 <span class="has-text-grey">(-35)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-36" /> ES512 <span class="has-text-grey">(-36)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-37" /> PS256 <span class="has-text-grey">(-37)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-47" /> ES256K <span class="has-text-grey">(-47)</span>
                        </label>
                    </div>
                    <div class="control" style="margin-top: 0.5rem">
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-48" /> ML-DSA-44 <span class="has-text-grey">(-48)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-49" /> ML-DSA-65 <span class="has-text-grey">(-49)</span>
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-algorithm" value="-50" /> ML-DSA-87 <span class="has-text-grey">(-50)</span>
                        </label>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">
                        <code>pubKeyCredParams</code>, ordered by preference &mdash; the client makes a
                        best-effort to create the most preferred type it can, and fails if it can create none
                        of them. Unchecking everything falls back to the library's defaults.
                        Level 3 recommends <em>against</em> offering the fully-specified
                        <code>-9</code>/<code>-19</code>/<code>-51</code>/<code>-52</code> here.
                    </p>
                    <p class="help">
                        The ML-DSA entries are the post-quantum algorithms RFC 9964 registers for COSE. This
                        server can verify them, but no shipping authenticator produces them yet, so expect the
                        client to fall through to whichever conventional algorithm you also offer &mdash; and
                        to fail outright if you offer nothing else.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <hr />
                <h3 class="is-size-6">WebAuthn Level 3</h3>

                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Hints</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-hint" value="security-key" /> security-key
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-hint" value="client-device" /> client-device
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-hint" value="hybrid" /> hybrid
                        </label>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">
                        &sect;5.8.8. Guides how the browser presents the ceremony, in the order checked here.
                        Hints are advisory &mdash; they do not restrict what the user may actually use. Setting a
                        hint also derives the authenticator attachment, so it takes precedence over the
                        Authenticator setting above.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Attestation formats</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-attestation-format" value="packed" /> packed
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-attestation-format" value="tpm" /> tpm
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox" style="margin-right: 1rem">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-attestation-format" value="apple" /> apple
                        </label>
                        <label class="checkbox">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="option-attestation-format" value="none" /> none
                        </label>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">
                        &sect;5.4. The attestation statement formats this Relying Party prefers, most preferred
                        first. Advisory: the authenticator may still use a format that is not listed. Only
                        meaningful when the attestation type above is not None.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Mediation</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-mediation">
                                <option selected value="">Optional (default)</option>
                                <option value="conditional">Conditional</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">
                        &sect;5.1.3. A conditional create is offered quietly by the browser rather than in a modal
                        prompt. Because no user presence test happens, the UP flag is not set and the server has
                        to know the ceremony was conditional in order to accept it.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="field">
                    <label class="checkbox">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="option-prf" /> Request the <code>prf</code> extension
                    </label>
                    <p class="help">
                        &sect;10.1.4. At registration this only asks whether the authenticator can evaluate a
                        pseudo-random function for this credential; the client reports the answer back as
                        <code>prf.enabled</code>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </form>

            <h3 class="is-size-6" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">This browser's client capabilities</h3>
            <p class="help">
                &sect;5.1.7. What <code>getClientCapabilities()</code> reports, so you can tell what is worth
                trying here.
            </p>
            <div id="client-capabilities" style="margin-top: 0.5rem"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>